  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Members_of_the_protection_system_in_verification">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#Members_of_the_personal_data_protection_system"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#authorization_for_international_transfer001">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Authorization_for_international_transfer"/>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:where_in_in_the_international_field_you_have_to_have rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#authorization_for_international_transfer001"/>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Excess_of_authorization>When in an international transfer an organization has many privileges</OntologiaLOPDP:Excess_of_authorization>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:General_detail>It is the permission you must have to perform an international data transfer.</OntologiaLOPDP:General_detail>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#delegate001">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Personal_data_delegate_in_verification"/>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:is_compliant_with_the_following_roles rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#delegate001"/>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Advise>Advises the data protection authority</OntologiaLOPDP:Advise>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Advise_on_risk_analysis>Advises the authority on risk analysis issues.</OntologiaLOPDP:Advise_on_risk_analysis>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Audit>Assists in audit processes and performs audits</OntologiaLOPDP:Audit>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Cooperate_with_the_Personal_Data_Protection_Authority>Cooperates with the authority</OntologiaLOPDP:Cooperate_with_the_Personal_Data_Protection_Authority>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Delegate_functions>Among its functions are:
- Advising the person in charge
- Supervising the Authority
- Advise on risk analysis
- Cooperate with the Authority</OntologiaLOPDP:Delegate_functions>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Details_of_the_law_details>Information</OntologiaLOPDP:Details_of_the_law_details>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:General_detail>It assists the data processor and data controller in specific cases and monitors them, performs auditing processes and collaborates with the authority to keep the other processes running smoothly.</OntologiaLOPDP:General_detail>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Name>Antonio</OntologiaLOPDP:Name>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Nature>The nature of its functions</OntologiaLOPDP:Nature>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Personal_detail>Helps the authority to fulfill its functions</OntologiaLOPDP:Personal_detail>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Personal_information>Delegate information</OntologiaLOPDP:Personal_information>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Purpose>These are the actions to be performed</OntologiaLOPDP:Purpose>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Scope>Scope of functions</OntologiaLOPDP:Scope>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Supervise>He/she is in charge of supervising when the manager's activities require supervision.</OntologiaLOPDP:Supervise>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Volume>Volume of data handled</OntologiaLOPDP:Volume>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#defense_of_claims001">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Claims_defense"/>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:segmented_into_the_following_international_cases rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#defense_of_claims001"/>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Claim_defense_details>Detail on defense claims in an international transfer case</OntologiaLOPDP:Claim_defense_details>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:General_detail>This is used when the data is subject to a defense of claims for a particular subject matter.</OntologiaLOPDP:General_detail>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#exceptions_for_transfers_or_international_communications001">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Exceptions_for_international_transfers_or_communications"/>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:as_to_the_national_and_international_related_to_it_be_held rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#exceptions_for_transfers_or_international_communications001"/>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Contract>There must be a contract</OntologiaLOPDP:Contract>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:General_detail>These are scenarios in which the owner's permission is not required to use his or her information.</OntologiaLOPDP:General_detail>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Informed>Exceptions to international transfer of the holder's data must be reported.</OntologiaLOPDP:Informed>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Legal_or_regulatory_obligation>International exceptions must have a legal or regulatory obligation</OntologiaLOPDP:Legal_or_regulatory_obligation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#teenagers001">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#Teenagers"/>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:and_as_your_age_will_have_to_be_of_your_age rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/franc/ontologies/2023/9/OntologiaLOPDP#teenagers001"/>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Access>Adolescent data must be accessible</OntologiaLOPDP:Access>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Anonymization>It must be possible to anonymize adolescent data.</OntologiaLOPDP:Anonymization>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Correction>Adolescent data must be able to be rectified</OntologiaLOPDP:Correction>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Disposal>It should be possible to delete teenage data</OntologiaLOPDP:Disposal>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:General_detail>In order to make use of their data, no detailed supervision is necessary, only the use to which the data will be put needs to be clearly stated. The age range to be considered as adolescent data is from 12 to 17 years old.</OntologiaLOPDP:General_detail>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Supervision>Teenagers can use their personal information without the need for adult consent, they do not need supervision, but the use that will be made of their data must be very clear.</OntologiaLOPDP:Supervision>
    <OntologiaLOPDP:Updated>Adolescent data must be updatable</OntologiaLOPDP:Updated>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/ley-organica-proteccion-datos-personales#before_dictating_corrective_measures">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
